            <h2>Galen Cassidy Peria</h2>
            <p class="muted">Galen Cassidy Peria is a New Orleans, LA based song-finder, wordsmith, film buff, histrionic, and excitable drinker. As a member of Vermont Joy Parade he toured the United States and Europe extensively between 2008&ndash;2014, starring alongside his bandmates (and Jared Leto) in the Vivian Strosberg documentary, &ldquo;The Clock Tick and The Heartbeat&rdquo;.</p>
            <p class="muted">In 2015 he helped found United Bakery Records and became one of their debut recording artists (in addition to &ldquo;The Tumbling Wheels&rdquo; and Shane Sayers) with his release of, &ldquo;Duke Aeroplane &amp; The Wrong Numbers: Higher Ground&rdquo;. He has previously collaborated with Hugh Mackey as lead actor in Mackey&rsquo;s 2010 feature film, &ldquo;Ties&rdquo;, and as actor and director with his own acclaimed short films, &ldquo;Elephant Shoes&rdquo; and &ldquo;Corporate Piracy&rdquo; (with Mackey as Director of Photography).</p>
          </div>
